Who: Titus Brown
When: February 5, 2016
Times: 9:15am-12:15pm PST
Where: DSI Space, Shield Library, UC Davis campus

Description:

This workshop will introduce the basics of git, a widely used system for
managing changes to files.  git and related systems are key for replicability
when doing any kind of computational analysis.

This will be a gentle introduction to git that follows the Software Carpentry
lesson, here,

